<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Domnall Brecc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 642</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Domnall Brecc was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> of the Cenél nGabráin, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedan-mac-gabrain">Áedán mac Gabráin</a>. He broke the alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> and was defeated at Mag Rath in Ireland in 637, losing Dál Riata's lands there. He suffered further defeats against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> and Britons and was killed by Owen of Strathclyde at Strathcarron in 642.</p></div>
